 "remarks": "Rare opportunity in Stamford's coveted Springdale neighborhood! Set on a private .26-acre corner lot with driveway access from a quiet, dead-end side street, this 1,173 sq. ft. two-bedroom home offers exceptional bones and an unbeatable location. Built in 1862 and renovated in 2005, the home is ready for its next chapter - hardwood floors lie beneath the wall-to-wall carpet on the main floor. The multi-level yard features a hidden private patio and a three-season porch, outdoor living at its best. Updated and fully renovated two-bedroom homes in the immediate area have recently sold between $560,000 and $828,000. Sold strictly as-is as part of an estate sale. Showings available only by appointment. Bring your vision and your contractor!",
